 "the_gate_refused_first": {
  "_note": "Worth recording because it is the safety property, not an obstacle. `runall.py` at the new default exited 2 without converting a single document: `gate.load_lane` compares the recorded profile_id against options.LANES and raises BaselineInvalid. A gate that had silently scored a PDFium run against PyMuPDF's record would have produced a full table of plausible regressions attributable to nothing.",
  "message": "invalid gate baseline: baseline lane 'product' is 'pymupdf/standard/libreoffice/refine3@240dpi', active profile is 'pdfium/standard/libreoffice/refine3@240dpi'; baseline lane 'raw' is 'pymupdf/standard/none/refine0@240dpi', active profile is 'pdfium/standard/none/refine0@240dpi'.",
  "consequence": "`--backend pymupdf` cannot be used to produce a gated 'before' either, and should not be: load_lane reads LANES, not the overridden options. The before column is therefore the FILE OF RECORD, and its continued validity is established by the control below rather than assumed."
 },
